          "heading": "Design context",
          "content": "## Design context\n\nConstruct separate gravity and wind force-transfer diagrams for a two-story steel school building with one braced bay per direction. Choose plausible grid dimensions and quantify floor tributary loads. Compare a rigid-diaphragm assumption with an explicitly flexible diaphragm. Deliver a drawing that identifies every collector and brace reaction; mark portions that require further engineering approval.\n\nA productive way to study this unit is to connect its smallest material or member model to the whole building. Every force has an entry point and an exit point; every brace must connect to a supporting system; and every design resistance belongs to a particular structural limit state. The educational calculations in this book aim to train reliable modeling judgment, not to automate sign-off. When the calculation appears simple, spend additional time determining whether the assumed support, material response and loading state can actually occur."
