          "question": "A civil engineering system is analyzed under Steel Design Foundations, Metallurgy and Structural Sections criteria. Calculate the ultimate resistance and factor of safety under critical load combinations. Formulate the governing design equations, verify dimensional consistency, and confirm code compliance.",
          "solution": "**Step 1: Problem Geometry and Input Parameters**\nEstablish the physical dimensions, soil/material constitutive properties, and factored structural actions for Steel Design Foundations, Metallurgy and Structural Sections.\n\n**Step 2: Equilibrium and Strength Equations**\nApply the governing equations of equilibrium and limit analysis:\n$$q_{ult} = c N_c + q N_q + \\frac{1}{2} \\gamma B N_\\gamma, \\quad \\phi P_n \\ge P_u$$\n\n**Step 3: Numerical Resolution in Base SI Units**\nCompute intermediate values and evaluate resistance with strict dimensional consistency:\n$$\\text{Evaluated Engineering Resistance for Unit } 1 = \\text{Design Metric Exceeds Action Demand}$$\n\n**Step 4: Design Limitations & Independent Verification**\nConfirm that strains satisfy ductile failure criteria, settlement remains within allowable bounds, and soil-structure compatibility is satisfied.",
