          "content": "## Numerical case studies\n\n### Case 8.1: Uniform corrosion sensitivity\n\n**Given:** Plate width=250 mm, initial thickness=14 mm, loss=0.04 mm/year per broad face, duration=25 years.\n\n**Computation:** Remaining thickness=14\u22122\u00d70.04\u00d725=12 mm; remaining area=3000 mm\u00b2.\n\n**Interpretation:** Localized pitting, environment and inspection data are excluded; assumed rate is not a service-life prediction.\n\n**Independent audit:** Before accepting the numerical answer, identify the dimension of the resulting quantity and confirm it matches the left-hand side of the formula. Replace the nominal input with an independently selected second input and repeat the calculation by hand. A single correct number can conceal an incorrect sign convention, wrong load level, or missing connection effect. State the physical phenomenon left outside the formula.\n\n### Case 8.2: Free steel thermal expansion\n\n**Given:** \u03b1=12\u00d710\u207b\u2076/\u00b0C, L=6500 mm, temperature rise=85\u00b0C.\n\n**Computation:** Free expansion \u03b1L\u0394T\u22486.63 mm.\n\n**Interpretation:** Restrained expansion may generate forces: free expansion alone cannot predict them.\n\n**Independent audit:** Before accepting the numerical answer, identify the dimension of the resulting quantity and confirm it matches the left-hand side of the formula. Replace the nominal input with an independently selected second input and repeat the calculation by hand. A single correct number can conceal an incorrect sign convention, wrong load level, or missing connection effect. State the physical phenomenon left outside the formula."
